1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
You replace the fuse.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
It blows again in minutes.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,500
Same accessory, same fuse,

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,000
dead again right after you swap it in.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,500
That can point to a short —

6
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,000
pulling more current than the circuit is rated for.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
A higher-amp fuse doesn't fix it —

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
it just lets more heat build up in the wiring.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,500
The circuit needs to be traced,

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,000
not the fuse upsized.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Worth checking before it becomes a bigger electrical repair.

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Stop by and we'll take a look — Nick's Tire & Auto.
